{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Privacy policy — extdir{% endblock %}
{% block meta_description %}How extdir handles personal data. Short version: almost none of it.{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<div class="wrap page">
    <div class="page-head">
        <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
        <p>Datenschutzerklärung under Art. 13 GDPR / DSGVO.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <p>
            extdir sets no cookies, runs no analytics, embeds nothing from third parties, and has no
            user accounts. Nothing is loaded from an external CDN, so browsing this site does not
            disclose your IP address to anyone but the server hosting it.
        </p>

        <h2>Controller</h2>
        <address>
            {{ operator.name }}<br>
            {{ operator.street }}<br>
            {{ operator.postalCity }}<br>
            {{ operator.country }}<br>
            <a href="mailto:{{ operator.email }}">{{ operator.email }}</a>
        </address>

        <h2>Server log files</h2>
        <p>
            The hosting provider records standard access logs when you request a page: IP address,
            timestamp, requested URL, referrer and user agent. This is technically necessary to
            deliver the site and to detect abuse.
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Legal basis:</strong> Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR — legitimate interest in operating and securing the service.</li>
            <li><strong>Retention:</strong> logs are deleted after 7 days unless needed to investigate a specific incident.</li>
            <li><strong>Recipients:</strong> the hosting provider, acting as processor under Art. 28 GDPR.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
        <p>
            None. There is no consent banner because there is nothing to consent to — no analytics,
            no advertising, no tracking pixels, no fingerprinting, no third-party embeds.
        </p>

        <h2>Search queries</h2>
        <p>
            Search terms are processed only to produce the results on the page. They are not stored,
            not profiled and not associated with you beyond the ordinary server log entry described
            above.
        </p>

        <h2>External links</h2>
        <p>
            Links to GitHub, Packagist and maintainer websites are ordinary links. Nothing from those
            services is loaded into this page, so no data reaches them until you actually click. Once
            you do, that site's own privacy policy applies.
        </p>

        <h2>Data we collect about extensions, not about you</h2>
        <p>
            The directory stores metadata about publicly published software packages: package names,
            descriptions, licences, version constraints, repository activity and maintainer links, all
            fetched from Packagist and GitHub. Where that metadata contains a maintainer's name or
            contact address, it is processed under Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR — the legitimate interest in
            operating a directory of open-source software, using information the maintainer chose to
            publish for exactly that purpose.
        </p>
        <p>
            If you are a maintainer and want your data removed, see the
            <a href="{{ path('takedown') }}">takedown policy</a>. Removal is not conditional on you
            giving a reason.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
            You have the right to access (Art. 15), rectification (Art. 16), erasure (Art. 17),
            restriction of processing (Art. 18), data portability (Art. 20) and to object to
            processing (Art. 21). Write to the address above. You also have the right to lodge a
            complaint with a supervisory authority; for North Rhine-Westphalia this is the
            Landesbeauftragte für Datenschutz und Informationsfreiheit NRW.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
            If this policy changes, the date below changes with it. There is no version history worth
            keeping while the answer to most questions remains “we do not collect that”.
        </p>

        <p class="small subtle" style="margin-top:2rem">
            Last updated: {{ 'now'|date('Y-m-d') }} ·
            <a href="{{ path('imprint') }}">Imprint</a> ·
            <a href="{{ path('terms') }}">Terms</a>
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
